  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adaptation investment pipeline for Fiji</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Active</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of this project is to unlock and accelerate significant climate finance for Fiji by developing a robust, ready-to-fund adaptation investment pipeline. This directly supports the implementation of the country&apos;s updated Nationally Determined Contribution (NDC). By completing the necessary technical and financial preparatory work, the project aims to reduce investment risk and transaction costs for potential donors. The successful realization of this objective will ensure that essential infrastructure and community adaptation measures are financed and deployed efficiently, promoting green growth and securing long-term resilience for Fijian communities against climate shocks.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is strategically designed to prepare a comprehensive and bankable adaptation investment pipeline for Fiji. This involves a sequence of technical and financial preparation activities to transition high-priority climate initiatives from initial concept into investment-ready documents. The scope includes identifying project needs across key sectors, conducting necessary feasibility studies, and packaging the projects to meet the rigorous standards of international donors. Furthermore, the description includes the crucial activity of resource mobilization, where the prepared pipeline is actively marketed to secure funding necessary for the full implementation of Fiji&#x2019;s adaptation priorities.</narrative>
  </description>
